laurel 2500: speaker audio on the Mi A3. TopazAudio keeps the ADSP PAS 1 boot, SMP2P, GLINK lpass edge, QRTR + pd-mapper of topaz; the Mi A3 firmware (ADSP.VT.5.4-00283-NICOBAR, modem partition) is Elite/APR, not AudioReach/GPR, so the GPR/WCD937x/SoundWire half is replaced: carveout 0x55300000+0x2200000; a FAT16 reader for image/adsp.* in modem_b (else modem_a); APR on apr_audio_svc (core state poll); AFE SEC_MI2S_RX (0x1002, IBIT 1.536 MHz, I2S SD0 48 kHz 16-bit stereo) <- ADM COPP (NULL topology) <- ASM session 1 (16-bit PCM writes, 8 x 20 ms periods from the pool, apps SMMU SID 0x41 identity, msw = SID low bits); MAX98927/MAX98937 amp at QUP0 SE1 I2C 0x3a (reset GPIO 95, vendor register maps, safe gains: no DSM); SEC_MI2S pins GPIO 125-128 function 2. sweet_i2c1 gets 16-bit register read/write. /dev/topaz-audio (+ /dev/redwood-audio of 0935) is made before the ADSP is up and drops frames while audio is off. On by default; kill switch adsp=0 or laurelaudio=0; one line LAUREL AUDIO: on|off: reason, after a self-check (path start with silence, the DSP must return 2 periods in 500 ms).

